(4,'Slow Internet','We are requesting for improved internet services within the company for better productivity.',1,216,'Other','Open','Medium',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]',NULL,'2025-03-19 16:32:35','2025-03-19 16:32:35',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(5,'Proposal for Extended Call Centre Hours to Enhance Customer Satisfaction and Revenue','I recommend introducing evening shifts for our call centre agents, with at least two agents working until 10 PM. This will allow us to better serve customers who are unavailable during regular hours, particularly after 6 PM, when we are losing potential business.\r\n\r\nImplementing this shift will improve customer satisfaction, capture missed opportunities, and drive revenue growth',1,216,'Workload & Scheduling','In Progress','Medium',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]',NULL,'2025-04-02 07:57:39','2025-04-02 15:11:53',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(6,'Proposal for Enhancing the Leave Application Process','I hope you’re doing well.\r\n\r\nI’d like to bring up two suggestions for brainstorming regarding how we apply for leave and delegate tasks. Currently, the process involves submitting a leave request through the HR system and then following up with an email detailing task delegation. While this works, I believe we can enhance efficiency by integrating the delegation process into the HR system itself.\r\n\r\nProposed Improvements:\r\n1️⃣ Integrated Task Delegation in the HR System – Instead of sending a separate email, employees could assign task delegation directly within the HR system when applying for leave. This way, all relevant team members can view the responsibilities in one place.\r\n\r\n2️⃣ Automated Notifications – The HR system could send notifications to the remaining team members and relevant stakeholders once a leave request is approved, ensuring that everyone is informed without the need for manual emails.\r\n\r\nBenefits:\r\nIncreased Efficiency – Reduces the time spent on follow-ups and emails, streamlining the leave process.\r\nBetter Transparency – Ensures all stakeholders have real-time visibility on task delegation.\r\nImproved Communication – Automated notifications prevent miscommunication or overlooked handovers.\r\nSeamless Workflow – Helps the team manage workloads more effectively in the absence of a team member.\r\n\r\nI’d love to hear your thoughts on this.',1,43,'Workload & Scheduling','Open','Medium',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]',NULL,'2025-04-03 17:24:47','2025-04-10 10:38:55','2025-04-10 10:38:55',NULL,NULL),
(7,'Proposal for Enhancing the Leave Application Process','I hope you’re doing well.\r\n\r\nI’d like to bring up two suggestions for brainstorming regarding how we apply for leave and delegate tasks. Currently, the process involves submitting a leave request through the HR system and then following up with an email detailing task delegation. While this works, I believe we can enhance efficiency by integrating the delegation process into the HR system itself.\r\n\r\nProposed Improvements:\r\n1️⃣ Integrated Task Delegation in the HR System – Instead of sending a separate email, employees could assign task delegation directly within the HR system when applying for leave. This way, all relevant team members can view the responsibilities in one place.\r\n\r\n2️⃣ Automated Notifications – The HR system could send notifications to the remaining team members and relevant stakeholders once a leave request is approved, ensuring that everyone is informed without the need for manual emails.\r\n\r\nBenefits:\r\nIncreased Efficiency – Reduces the time spent on follow-ups and emails, streamlining the leave process.\r\nBetter Transparency – Ensures all stakeholders have real-time visibility on task delegation.\r\nImproved Communication – Automated notifications prevent miscommunication or overlooked handovers.\r\nSeamless Workflow – Helps the team manage workloads more effectively in the absence of a team member.\r\n\r\nI’d love to hear your thoughts on this.',1,43,'Workload & Scheduling','Closed','Medium',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]',NULL,'2025-04-03 17:24:59','2025-06-05 07:07:22',NULL,NULL,NULL);
